nodecode-cognee is a rewrite of topoteretes's topoteretes/cognee-integrations:

  https://github.com/topoteretes/cognee-integrations
  commit b132740960181e712f15c76ee80519cbd15fdb5d
  Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2025 topoteretes (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is integrations/hermes-agent of that commit. Its four
portable tools keep their names, descriptions and parameters (cognee_recall,
cognee_remember, cognee_forget, cognee_switch_dataset), its HTTP transport
keeps its wire (X-Api-Key whenever a key is set; POST /api/v1/recall with
query, top_k, datasets and the graph scope; the multipart POST
/api/v1/remember with run_in_background; POST /api/v1/forget by dataset or
by datasetId + dataId; GET /api/v1/datasets and its data pages), and its
behaviour is carried over: one recall never reads the session cache, a
document is named after its content so identical content is the server's
no-op, forgetting is two-phase with confirm=true and the original's caps (100
documents scanned, 8 candidates, 240-character previews), and an item with
no readable text is a miss rather than a hit.

What was left out, and why: the local-server mode, which downloads and
installs the cognee package from PyPI into a private Python venv (a Lisp cell
bundles no Python, so base_url names a server the user started or a remote
one); the per-turn capture and the session-end improve() bridge, because the
Nodecode seam that reads standing sections once per turn carries no
per-message payload, so the model calls cognee_remember instead; the
code-graph lane and the recap tool, which read repositories indexed by the
original's CLI and the harness's session table; and the prompt decorations
(the system-prompt block, the memory-hit counter and the "> Cognee:" credit
line), which are Hermes prompt text rather than a tool. LICENSE is the
repository's LICENSE, unchanged.
